WEBVTT

NOTE Ledger short walkthrough captions for docs/assets/ledger-walkthrough-short.webm
NOTE Silent screen cut (~136s) from Phase 6 capture; captions are the narrative track.
NOTE Synthetic seeded data only. Stripe is an optional test-mode evidence feed.

00:00.000 --> 00:05.500
Ledger: a production-shaped SaaS revenue investigation agent.

00:05.500 --> 00:12.000
Synthetic seed data for review - not a live customer environment.

00:12.000 --> 00:20.000
Problem: week-over-week paid MRR dropped after failed renewals.

00:20.000 --> 00:28.000
Published agent versions snapshot prompt, model, tools, and scopes.

00:28.000 --> 00:38.000
Fork a version to change capabilities without rewriting history.

00:38.000 --> 00:44.000
Tool registry: typed schemas, one implementation, one permission scope.

00:44.000 --> 00:49.000
Runtime policy requires both an enabled tool id and an allowed scope.

00:49.000 --> 00:58.000
Launch the seeded MRR-drop incident. Ordered steps and tool calls persist.

00:58.000 --> 01:06.000
Root cause names failed-renewal evidence and affected accounts.

01:06.000 --> 01:10.000
Every major claim cites SQL, tickets, or docs. Trace and cost sit with the report.

01:10.000 --> 01:15.000
Safety: customer follow-up stays a mock. High-risk actions need approval.

01:15.000 --> 01:20.000
Reject or approve is recorded. Rejection is terminal and audited.

01:20.000 --> 01:29.000
Observability: success rate, p95 latency, and estimated cost per version.

01:29.000 --> 01:38.000
Aggregates drill back into individual runs - not a vanity dashboard.

01:38.000 --> 01:48.000
Eval Studio runs the same six seeded cases against a published version.

01:48.000 --> 01:58.000
A-vs-B: remove a required evidence tool and a pass becomes a regression.

01:58.000 --> 02:04.000
Release risk is visible case-by-case, not hidden in an average score.

02:04.000 --> 02:09.500
Optional Stripe test-mode can feed billing evidence into Ledger records.

02:09.500 --> 02:12.500
Test-mode only, ingestion only - no live credentials, no checkout.

02:12.500 --> 02:15.840
Claim: cited evidence, approval gates, traces, and regression detection - not fluent prose alone.
